51" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $a\\ne 0$, we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false while statement III is true. Simplifying the expression $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+b\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot b & =-a\\cdot a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0$, we obtain that $-a\\cdot a<0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4876d8775b8a0e6807996278b34b2b1a89e06bcfb58cf6c739679b9762979c1"} {"question" "q-74051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044469/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cbcd6ef36778884ab630315463abd36bcdeb577db51f2b607199560a788a8240"} {"question" "q-74051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4876d8775b8a0e6807996278b34b2b1a89e06bcfb58cf6c739679b9762979c1"} {"question" "q-74051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044469/state.json" "file_sha256" "e4876d8775b8a0e6807996278b34b2b1a89e06bcfb58cf6c739679b9762979c1"} {"question" "q-74051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:a